<p>
Jason Snell has <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/07/apple-tv-is-essentially-dead-no-long-live-apple-tv/">a few words</a> to say about Dan Rayburns&rsquo;s post on LinkedIn concerning <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/danrayburn_appletv-streamingmedia-svod-share-7482437576889585664-3tsx/">the price increase for Apple TV and why it spells the end of the device</a>. I, too, have a couple of things to say.
</p>
<p>
First, when did LinkedIn become a social network? I thought it was supposed to be a place where job seekers and employers could find each other. I first became aware of its descent into silliness last year when Watts Martin <a href="https://tracks.ranea.org/post/780817630854578176/the-robots-have-come-for-your-em-dashes">informed us that, according to &ldquo;LinkedIn influencers&rdquo;, real people don&rsquo;t use em-dashes</a>. Martin and I had a good chuckle but even at the time I wondered <a href="https://irreal.org/blog/?p=12921">what a LinkedIn influencer could possibly be</a>. Now, apparently, LinkedIn is a place where anyone can advance any nonsense they please.
</p>
<p>
Second, everyone writing about Apple&rsquo;s recent price increases keeps ignoring the fact that they were driven by AI-fed RAM increases that are out of Apple&rsquo;s control. You can argue that the 50% increases were out of bounds but, again: RAM prices.
</p>
<p>
Third, I think Rayburn&rsquo;s whole argument is silly. If you belong to the Applesphere, you&rsquo;re used to high prices. Some iPhones are approaching \$1,000, a top-of-the-line iWatch is about \$800, and even before the increases, MacBook Pros were pricey. I&rsquo;m pretty sure few Apple users are going to complain about \$250 for an Apple TV.
</p>
<p>
Finally, Apple TV is more than just a streaming device. Here at the Irreal bunker we do little streaming but have a top-of-the-line Apple TV. Why? Because it&rsquo;s the hub for the bunker&rsquo;s Smart Home system. It basically runs the bunker&rsquo;s nerve system<sup><a id="fnr.1" class="footref" href="#fn.1" role="doc-backlink">1</a></sup>. If it didn&rsquo;t stream at all we wouldn&rsquo;t care. It still runs the household automation.
</p>
